# Derived term index (QHOP02, 2026-10-07): build_site.write_glossary_index
# rewrites it from data/glossary.json on every build (nightly and CI run
# build_site.py), so tracking it would only add a merge conflict per glossary edit.
data/glossary_index.json
# Slim quick-search index (QHOP06): mlb_player_export.write_player_search,
# beside player_links.json in the same d9b2 step.
data/player_search.json
# Source-vs-source backtest output (regenerated each monthly run; powers the
# Methodology & Track Record tab). Generated artifact, like timeseries.json.
data/source_backtest.json
# The PUBLIC BETTING RECORD and its two sidecars, untracked 2026-08-09 because
# tracking them is what destroyed the record. deploy/nightly-build.sh runs
# `git checkout -- .` before every pipeline, so a row appended on production at
# 21:00 was reverted to the committed `[]` at 03:10 the next morning with no
# error anywhere: load_record read the restored file as "the record is empty"
# and check_append_only then waved the same one-row proposal through as a legal
# append. The immutability check held on every write and the ledger still could
# not survive a night.
#
# The SOURCE OF TRUTH is now .cache/betting/record.jsonl (append-only, one JSON
# object per line, chain-hashed, untracked via `.cache/` at the top of this
# file). data/betting_record.json is a DERIVED re-render written by every build
# and published by rsync; losing it costs nothing. The two sidecars are derived
# the same way, from the record plus the odds cache and the completed games.
data/betting_record.json
data/betting_clv.json
data/betting_settlement.json
# The PAPER-BET LEDGER, on the same reasoning one level down. This file was
# untracked AND unignored, which is the worst of the three states: `git checkout
# -- .` could not touch it, and a single `git add -A` would have tracked it and
# armed the identical defect on the evidence base gate 3 is counting toward.
# Source of truth is .cache/betting/shadow.json (untracked via `.cache/`, on the
# backup list in deploy/WEBMASTER.md); this copy is a derived re-render written
# by every write and published by rsync because data_catalog advertises it.
data/betting_shadow.json
# The FUTURES FORWARD RECORD, on exactly the same reasoning. It landed untracked
# AND unignored on 2026-09-06, the state the note above calls the worst of the
# three, and it is an accruing file: one entry per day, and the whole point is
# that a completed season can be scored against the numbers that were live
# through it. `git checkout -- .` at 03:10 would revert every entry the night
# before had added. Source of truth is .cache/futures/ledger.json (untracked via
# `.cache/`, on the backup list in deploy/WEBMASTER.md); this copy is a derived
# re-render written by every build and published by rsync.
data/futures_ledger.json
# The POSTSEASON BRACKET SIMULATOR (docs/betting-2026-10/BRACKET_SIM_GATE.md),
# on the same two reasonings. Its payload is a nightly build product like
# data/futures.json beside it, and its forward record is an accruing file whose
# source of truth is .cache/bracket_sim/record.json; the data/ copy is a derived
# re-render published by rsync, never tracked, because the nightly
# `git checkout -- .` would revert every day's entry (gate 7.2, BS-1 (a)).
data/bracket_sim.json
data/bracket_sim_record.json
# The TRADE PARTNER SCREEN's public chain index (docs/trademachine-2026-10/
# TRADE_PARTNER_SCREEN_GATE.md 3.2): hashes only, re-rendered every night
# from .cache/trade_partner_screen/record/chain.json, the source of truth,
# and published by rsync. Untracked for the bracket record's reason.
data/trade_partner_screen_chain.json
# The LEARNING SERIES, derived the same way from the eval, the two ledgers and
# its own append-only history. Rewritten by run_monthly step 9e every night.
data/betting_learning.json
# Resolved headshot-context map (regenerated by headshots.py each run; drives
# the prospect-photo fallback chain). Generated artifact.
data/photo_ctx.json
# v31.12 — pitch_plot sidecar (raw per-pitch coordinates for the
# detail-page chart). 100+ MB at full pipeline rebuild; over GitHub's
# 100 MB single-file ceiling. Generated by storage.export_timeseries_json.
data/pitch_plots.json
# v32 — split per player (data/pitch_plots/{key}.json, ~450KB each);
# same generated-artifact policy as the monolith it replaces.
data/pitch_plots/
# v33 — player_detail per-player sidecar (spray/rolling-xwOBA coordinates,
# game logs, historical per-source tools). Generated by export_timeseries_json.
data/player_detail/
# v47 - per-graduate full-record shards (data/debuts_full/{key}.json), regenerated
# by every full export; the graduate card fetches these instead of debuts.json
data/debuts_full/
# Q9_22a - per-player MLB transaction events (data/mlb_events/<mlbam>.json,
# index.json, recent.json), written by mlb_events.py once MLB_EVENTS_LIVE is
# on; regenerated nightly by run_daily step 9e-pre0g.
data/mlb_events/
# Q8_11 - the /mlbstats/ drawer's per-player game files (data/mlbstats_player/
# <mlbam>.json), written by mlbstats_rolling_export.py once MLBSTATS_DRAWER_LIVE
# is on; regenerated nightly by run_daily step 9e-pre0h.
data/mlbstats_player/
# QMLP01 - one MLB player card per file (data/mlb_player_detail/<key>.json),
# written beside data/mlb_player_detail.json by mlb_player_export.py.
data/mlb_player_detail/
# FanGraphs CSV drop folder — user-supplied exports + processed archive
data/fangraphs_imports/
# Baseball America drop folder - owner-supplied board pastes + processed archive.
# NEVER commit and NEVER deploy: BA boards are licensed subscription material used
# here only as model TRAINING input, never as displayed content. Ignoring the tree
# keeps it out of git and, because deploy/nightly-build.sh only rsyncs data/*.json
# at depth 1, out of the public webroot as well. If a derived artifact is ever
# written from this data it must be added to deploy/data_exclude.txt in the same
# commit and may not be a model_registry eval_artifact (test_publish_manifest.py).
data/baseballamerica_imports/
# Tracked exception to the global *.csv ignore: scraped FanGraphs ARTICLE
# boards (e.g. Marlins 2026 Top 53). FanGraphs is Cloudflare-blocked so the
# deploy box can't re-scrape, and these aren't otherwise reproducible — commit
# them so run_monthly._stage_fangraphs_articles re-ingests them every build.
!data/fangraphs_articles/
!data/fangraphs_articles/*.csv

